    {
      "id": "definition",
      "duration": 10.6,
      "narration": "Latency is how long you wait for something to arrive. It is not how much data you can move at once. That is bandwidth. Latency is how long the very first bit takes to get there.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "icon",
          "name": "user",
          "x": 15,
          "y": 45,
          "size": 18,
          "draw": 0.8,
          "id": "you",
          "label": "you",
          "start": 0.3
        },
        {
          "type": "icon",
          "name": "server",
          "x": 85,
          "y": 45,
          "size": 18,
          "draw": 0.8,
          "id": "server",
          "label": "server",
          "start": 3.2
        },
        {
          "type": "arrow",
          "from": "you",
          "to": "server",
          "draw": 0.6,
          "label": "latency: how LONG it takes",
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "start": 6.1
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "bandwidth: how MUCH fits at once",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 85,
          "size": 5,
          "draw": 1.0,
          "color": "#1e6fd9",
          "start": 8.8
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "numbers",
      "duration": 9.1,
      "narration": "Every computer is a chain of places where data can live, and each one is slower than the one before. These are the numbers every developer should know.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Latency numbers every developer should know",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 12,
          "size": 6,
          "draw": 1.4,
          "start": 0.3
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "x": 22,
          "y": 30,
          "size": 5.5,
          "spacing": 1.7,
          "draw": 5,
          "items": [
            "CPU cache:  1 nanosecond",
            "Memory (RAM):  100 nanoseconds",
            "SSD read:  0.1 milliseconds",
            "Server in the same data center:  0.5 ms",
            "Hard disk seek:  10 ms",
            "Round trip across the ocean:  150 ms"
          ],
          "start": 3.3
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scale",
      "duration": 8.3,
      "narration": "Those numbers are too small to feel, so let's stretch time. Imagine reading from the CPU cache took one second.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "If reading the CPU cache took 1 second...",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 8,
          "size": 5.5,
          "draw": 1.2,
          "start": 0.3
        },
        {
          "type": "icon",
          "name": "cpu",
          "x": 12,
          "y": 22,
          "size": 9,
          "draw": 0.6,
          "id": "row0",
          "start": 2.77
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
