    {
      "id": "trips",
      "duration": 8.1,
      "narration": "Now look at what a single page load really costs. Before the first byte of the page arrives, your browser has to make several round trips.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Round trips before the first byte",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 10,
          "size": 6,
          "draw": 1.2,
          "start": 0.3
        },
        {
          "type": "icon",
          "name": "monitor",
          "x": 10,
          "y": 50,
          "size": 14,
          "draw": 0.8,
          "id": "browser",
          "label": "browser",
          "start": 3.1
        },
        {
          "type": "icon",
          "name": "server",
          "x": 90,
          "y": 50,
          "size": 14,
          "draw": 0.8,
          "id": "site",
          "label": "server",
          "start": 6.0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "handshakes",
      "duration": 6.1,
      "narration": "One to look up the address with D N S. One to open the connection. One or two for the encryption handshake. And one for the request itself.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "list",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "size": 5.5,
          "spacing": 1.9,
          "draw": 5,
          "items": [
            "1. DNS lookup",
            "2. Open the connection (TCP)",
            "3. Encryption handshake (TLS)",
            "4. The request itself (HTTP)"
          ],
          "start": 0.3
        }
      ],
      "keepPrevious": true
    },
    {
      "id": "cost",
      "duration": 4.5,
      "narration": "Four round trips at a hundred milliseconds each is almost half a second, and not a single pixel has been drawn yet.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "4 trips x 100 ms = 400 ms",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 86,
          "size": 6.5,
          "draw": 1.0,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "id": "total",
          "start": 0.3
        },
        {
          "type": "ring",
          "target": "total",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "start": 2.9
        }
      ],
      "keepPrevious": true
    },
    {
      "id": "bandwidth",
      "duration": 9.9,
      "narration": "This is why a faster internet plan often changes almost nothing. For most web pages, doubling your bandwidth barely helps. Cutting round trips does.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "box",
          "id": "more",
          "label": "2x bandwidth",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 40,
          "w": 46,
          "h": 18,
          "draw": 0.8,
          "start": 0.3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "barely faster",
          "x": 28,
          "y": 66,
          "size": 6,
          "draw": 1.0,
          "color": "#666666",
          "start": 3.0
        },
        {
          "type": "box",
          "id": "fewer",
          "label": "fewer round trips",
          "x": 72,
          "y": 40,
          "w": 52,
          "h": 18,
          "fill": "#d3f9d8",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "start": 5.4
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "much faster",
          "x": 72,
          "y": 66,
          "size": 6,
          "draw": 1.0,
          "color": "#2a9d4b",
          "start": 8.1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "loop",
      "duration": 10.6,
      "narration": "The same thing happens inside your own system. Code that runs a database query inside a loop pays a full round trip for every single item.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "icon",
          "name": "code",
          "x": 16,
          "y": 45,
          "size": 18,
          "draw": 0.8,
          "id": "app",
