    },
    {
      "id": "batch",
      "duration": 7.1,
      "narration": "A hundred queries at one millisecond each is a tenth of a second, wasted. One query that asks for all hundred rows at once takes about one millisecond.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "100 queries x 1 ms = 100 ms",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 32,
          "size": 7,
          "draw": 1.0,
          "color": "#c0392b",
          "start": 0.3
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "1 query for 100 rows = about 1 ms",
          "x": 50,
          "y": 58,
          "size": 7,
          "draw": 1.0,
          "color": "#2a9d4b",
          "id": "batched",
          "start": 2.9
        },
        {
          "type": "ring",
          "target": "batched",
          "draw": 0.8,
          "color": "#2a9d4b",
          "start": 5.5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tail",
      "duration": 7.1,
      "narration": "There is one more trap, and it is a big one. Averages lie. What your users feel is the slowest requests, the ninety ninth percentile.",
      "elements": [
        {
          "type": "icon",
